# Repository-wide shellcheck configuration.
#
# The lint job runs shellcheck at --severity=info over every tracked *.sh. info
# is the level at which SC2086 (unquoted expansion) becomes visible; warning is
# not enough, which is the whole reason for running below error at all.
#
# Two checks are disabled repository-wide because every occurrence here is the
# intended form, and leaving them on would train people to ignore the output:
#
#   SC2016  "expressions don't expand in single quotes". Ours are printf format
#           strings that deliberately contain literal backticks and %s, and
#           `bash -c 'f "$1"' _ "$arg"` where $1 must expand in the inner shell.
#   SC1091  "not following <source>". The sourced files are per-case data
#           (cases/*/case.conf), not code to analyse.
#
# Anything else stays on. Suppress a genuine one-off at the line, with a reason.
disable=SC2016,SC1091
